This is a research commission: do not make a web page.
Send the researcher subagent to look it up, then write the findings in English as two files.
"summary.md": a three-sentence summary first, then the key points as a list, each point followed by the numbers of its sources in brackets, such as [1][3], then the sources, numbered, with their links.
"sources.json": JSON, {"sources": [{"n": 1, "title": "the page's title", "url": "https://...", "checked": "YYYY-MM-DD, the day you looked", "quote": "a short line from the page (optional)"}], "unsourced": ["each conclusion you found no source for, word for word"]}.
Every key point needs at least one number. A conclusion you found no source for goes into "unsourced", and in the summary it is marked "no source found" instead of a number.
Never make up a link or a source: use only pages the search found or you opened this time.
Say plainly where sources disagree or where you are unsure.

